Replaced by the engine or by the design (no counterpart by intent)
------------------------------------------------------------------
The DMA routines and the VRAM queue: what they carried goes to the engine's
tiles, maps, palette and sprite table directly (race_vram_write routes a
VRAM destination to its role).
  7E:ABB6 VramDmaFromBank7F -> race_vram_write
  7E:ABD7 VramDmaFromGsuRam -> race_vram_write
  7E:AC08 VramDmaRowsFromGsuRam -> race_vram_write
  7E:ACF7 OamDma -> sprites.c OamDmaAll (the sprite table is the engine's)
  7E:B0F6 CgramDma -> palette.c CgramDmaAll, RasterPaletteUpload
  03:ECA8 DmaFromDescriptor -> race_video.c clear_all (its only use, VideoStartUploads)
  7F:08C7 VramDmaWideRowsFromGsuRam -> none: the two-player pictures' rows;
         both pictures are in the engine's draw list (race_two_player_list),
         race/flow.c two_player_rows keeps only the stages' order
  7E:A7C9 NmiFrameUploadRace -> race/flow.c race_frame_upload (the race
         session's), the stages by role
  0B:F567 WindowHdmaChannelsSetup -> menu/screens.c ChampionScreenOpen (the
         menus session's per-line tables)
  03:ED7F GradientFillCgadd -> picture.c race_lines_send: the gradient is a
         per-line table of colour 0, so the CGADD table it fills has no
         counterpart (its caller RaceHudSetup leaves it to the video side)

Converted by other sessions, with the code that drives them
------------------------------------------------------------
  7E:A7BE NmiFrameUpload -> race/flow.c race_frame_upload (the race session's)
  07:C683 OverlayFramesUntilFaded -> race/results.c, one frame of it per
         update (the race session's)

Dead
----
Proof, for each: the original's own record says nothing reaches it ("Nothing
in the game calls it", "Nothing jumps to it or calls it", "nothing branches
to", "Nothing reaches it", "No caller found", "Nothing calls it in the
traces"), and the cartridge (assets/cart.dat) holds no JSR or JMP to its
address in its bank or the RAM code's block, no JSL or JML to it, and no
pointer word to it (the counts are all 0). The routine catalog lists most of
them as run: the unit scripts call them directly, which the game never does.
  7E:A7F3 VramRowsCopyUnused
  03:ECBE VramClearWords
